def longest_palindrome(s: str) -> str:
    if not s:
        return ""

    start, end = 0, 0  # inclusive bounds of best palindrome found

    def expand(left: int, right: int):
        """Expand around center while palindrome holds; return (l, r) inclusive."""
        while left >= 0 and right < len(s) and s[left] == s[right]:
            left -= 1
            right += 1
        return left + 1, right - 1

    for i in range(len(s)):
        # Odd-length palindrome centered at i
        l1, r1 = expand(i, i)
        if r1 - l1 > end - start:
            start, end = l1, r1

        # Even-length palindrome centered between i and i+1
        l2, r2 = expand(i, i + 1)
        if r2 - l2 > end - start:
            start, end = l2, r2

    return s[start:end + 1]
```

This uses the expand-around-center technique in O(n²) time and O(1) extra space. Since we only update the result when a strictly longer palindrome is found (`>` comparison), the earliest-starting palindrome wins in case of ties.

