def longest_palindrome(s):
    if not s:
        return ""
    best_start, best_len = 0, 1

    def expand(left, right):
        nonlocal best_start, best_len
        while left >= 0 and right < len(s) and s[left] == s[right]:
            length = right - left + 1
            # strictly longer only; ties keep earlier start
            if length > best_len:
                best_start, best_len = left, length
            left -= 1
            right += 1

    for i in range(len(s)):
        expand(i, i)       # odd length
        expand(i, i + 1)   # even length

    return s[best_start:best_start + best_len]
```

This expands around each center (2n−1 centers), and since expansions happen in order of increasing starting index, ties naturally keep the earliest-starting palindrome. Time complexity: O(n²).

